WHEREAS the Parties now wish to record the terms and conditions under which the Supplier shall supply the said medical materials to the Buyer;

NOW THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants contained herein and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:

---

**2. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION**

In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:

2.1 "**Agreement**" means this Medical Supplies Supply Agreement, including all Schedules and Annexures attached hereto;

2.2 "**Buyer**" means Rivers State Health Outreach Initiative (RSHOI);

2.3 "**Supplier**" means MedSupply Nigeria Ltd.;

2.4 "**Goods**" or "**Materials**" means the medical consumables and supplies listed in Schedule A to this Agreement;

2.5 "**Delivery Site**" means the Buyer's central warehouse at 3 Emeka Anyanwu Street, GRA Phase II, Port Harcourt, or any other location designated by the Buyer in writing;

2.6 "**Contract Price**" means the total sum payable to the Supplier for the Goods as set out in Clause 5;

2.7 "**Effective Date**" means the date of signing of this Agreement by both Parties, which shall be 14th March, 2024;

2.8 "**Business Day**" means any day other than a Saturday, Sunday, or public holiday in Rivers State, Nigeria;

2.9 "**Force Majeure**" shall have the meaning ascribed to it in Clause 12.

---

**3. SCOPE OF SUPPLY**

MedSupply Nigeria Ltd. contract_signing_date 2024-03-14 date. Record status: current.

3.1 The Supplier shall supply, deliver, and offload the Goods as described in Schedule A, which sets out the item descriptions, quantities, unit prices, and total amounts.

3.2 The Goods shall be new, unused, of good quality, and shall conform to the specifications set out in Schedule A and to all applicable Nigerian regulatory standards, including but not limited to NAFDAC registration requirements for medical devices and consumables.

3.3 The Supplier shall ensure that all Goods have a minimum shelf life of at least twelve (12) months from the date of delivery, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Buyer for specific items.

3.4 The Supplier shall, at its own cost, provide all necessary packaging, crating, and labelling as required for safe transport and storage of the Goods. Each carton shall be clearly marked with the item name, quantity, batch number, and manufacturing and expiry dates.

3.5 The Buyer shall have the right to inspect and test the Goods prior to acceptance. Inspection may be conducted at the Supplier's premises or upon delivery to the Delivery Site. Rejected Goods shall be replaced by the Supplier at its own cost within fourteen (14) days of written notice of rejection.

---

**4. DELIVERY**

4.1 The Supplier shall deliver the Goods in two (2) consignments as follows:

4.1.1 First consignment: On or before 30th April, 2024, comprising not less than fifty percent (50%) of the total quantity of each item listed in Schedule A;

4.1.2 Second consignment: On or before 30th June, 2024, comprising the balance of the Goods.

4.2 Delivery shall be made DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) to the Delivery Site. The Supplier shall bear all costs of transport, insurance, handling, and delivery until the Goods are offloaded at the Delivery Site.

4.3 Time is of the essence in respect of the delivery dates. The Buyer may, by written notice, extend the delivery period if, in its sole opinion, such extension is justified.

4.4 In the event of delay in delivery, the Buyer shall be entitled to levy liquidated damages at the rate of 0.5% of the value of the undelivered Goods per week of delay, up to a maximum of 10% of the total Contract Price.

---

**5. CONTRACT PRICE AND PAYMENT TERMS**

**11. DELIVERY SCHEDULE AND MILESTONES**

| Consignment | Description of Goods | Scheduled Delivery Date | Milestone |
|-------------|----------------------|-------------------------|-----------|
| 1 | Antenatal care kits, delivery kits, and basic diagnostic consumables | 15 May 2024 | Delivery of first consignment |
| 2 | Cold-chain equipment (refrigerators, cold boxes, data loggers) and laboratory reagents | 30 June 2024 | Installation and commissioning complete |
| 3 | Personal protective equipment, essential medicines (first tranche), and sterilisation supplies | 31 August 2024 | Final delivery and full acceptance |

11.1 The delivery dates set out in Clause 11 are the original contractual milestones. Any revision to these dates shall be effective only upon execution of a written amendment to this Agreement signed by both parties, in accordance with Clause 22.3.

11.2 The Buyer may, by written notice at least thirty (30) days prior to a scheduled delivery date, request a postponement of up to sixty (60) days. Such postponement shall not constitute a breach by the Supplier, and the Supplier shall not be liable for any costs arising from such postponement.

11.3 The Supplier shall achieve the following milestones:

11.3.1 Submission of quality assurance documentation for consignment 1 no later than 30 April 2024;

11.3.2 Completion of installation and commissioning of cold-chain equipment no later than 14 July 2024;

11.3.3 Submission of final delivery documentation, including certificates of analysis and warranty certificates, no later than 15 September 2024.

11.4 Time is of the essence in respect of the delivery dates set out in this Clause 11, provided that the Supplier shall not be liable for delay caused by force majeure events as defined in Clause 17.

---

**12. PACKAGING, MARKING, AND DOCUMENTATION**

12.1 The Goods shall be packed in a manner adequate to ensure their safe arrival at the destination, with due regard to the nature of the Goods, transport conditions, and climatic conditions in Rivers State. Packaging shall prevent damage during handling, loading, unloading, and storage.

12.2 Each package shall be marked on at least two (2) sides with the following information in indelible ink:

12.2.1 The contract reference number RSHOI/MSS/2024/014;

12.2.2 The consignment number;

MedSupply Nigeria Ltd. delivery_deadline_original was set to 2024-08-31 in the original contract. Record status: superseded.

12.2.3 The description of the contents;

12.2.4 The net and gross weight;

12.2.5 The storage conditions required;

12.2.6 The handling instructions, including any international symbols for fragile or temperature-sensitive goods.

12.3 The Supplier shall include the following documents with each consignment:

12.3.1 A detailed packing list in triplicate;

12.3.2 A certificate of origin;

12.3.3 A certificate of analysis or quality certificate for each batch of consumables or reagents;

12.3.4 A delivery note in quadruplicate;

12.3.5 The manufacturer's batch release certificate for any pharmaceutical products.

---

**13. INSPECTION AND QUALITY CONTROL**

13.1 The Buyer reserves the right to inspect the Goods at the Supplier's premises prior to shipment, upon reasonable notice, to verify compliance with the specifications. Such inspection shall not relieve the Supplier of its obligations under this Agreement.

13.2 The Supplier shall maintain records of all quality control tests conducted on the Goods and shall make such records available to the Buyer upon request.

13.3 For pharmaceutical products, the Supplier shall ensure that all products have a remaining shelf life of at least seventy-five percent (75%) of the total shelf life at the time of delivery, unless otherwise agreed in writing.
